1
00:06:56,000 --> 00:07:02,000
The story of a boy suddenly alone in the world. The men who
challenge him. And the girl who helps him become a man.

2
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:58,000
The Man from Snowy River is a drama, romance,
adventure film directed by George T. Miller.

3
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:54,000
Jim Craig has lived his first 18 years in the
mountains of Australia on his father's farm.

4
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:50,000
The death of his father forces him to go to the lowlands to earn
enough money to get the farm back on its feet.

5
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:46,000
Jim Craig, played by Tom Burlinson.

6
00:41:36,000 --> 00:41:42,000
Jessica Harrison, played by Sigrid Thornton.

7
00:48:32,000 --> 00:48:38,000
Henry Craig, played by Terence Donovan.

8
00:55:28,000 --> 00:55:34,000
Harrison / Spur, played by Kirk Douglas.

9
01:02:24,000 --> 01:02:30,000
Clancy, played by Jack Thompson.

10
01:09:20,000 --> 01:09:26,000
Mountain Man, played by Tommy Dysart.

11
01:16:16,000 --> 01:16:22,000
The Man from Snowy River is a 1982 Australian Western drama film based on the Banjo Paterson poem "The Man from Snowy River." The film stars Kirk Douglas in dual roles as the brothers Harrison (a character who appeared
frequently in Paterson's poems) and Spur, Jack Thompson as Clancy, Tom Burlinson as Jim Craig, Sigrid Thornton as Harrison's daughter Jessica, Terence Donovan as Jim's father, Henry Craig, and Chris Haywood as Curly.

12
01:23:12,000 --> 01:23:18,000
Both Burlinson and Thornton later reprised their roles in the 1988 sequel, The Man
from Snowy River II, which was distributed by Walt Disney Pictures.

13
01:30:08,000 --> 01:30:14,000
The film explores themes of australia, regret, horseback riding, river, horse.

14
01:37:04,000 --> 01:37:10,000
The tone is emotional.
